Wellby: It's a top.

04:29:19.310 --> 04:29:20.610
Delwath: Um, hey, Dim. By the way...

04:29:21.790 --> 04:29:23.130
Unknown: Wait, did I do see invisible?

04:29:23.510 --> 04:29:24.430
Unknown: Did I do see invisible?

04:29:25.950 --> 04:29:26.310
Seeker: When?

04:29:28.950 --> 04:29:29.090
Unknown: Like,

04:29:30.030 --> 04:29:31.150
Delwath: uh, when we started combat.

04:29:31.810 --> 04:29:33.030
Delwath: No, I didn't. I'm gonna say it wasn't.

04:29:33.030 --> 04:29:34.850
DM: You did it with the... You only did it in the-

04:29:35.530 --> 04:29:35.790
Unknown: I mean-

04:29:35.790 --> 04:29:36.490
Unknown: ... vests

04:29:36.490 --> 04:29:37.510
Delwath: ... it only lasts for an hour,

04:29:38.990 --> 04:29:40.330
Unknown: but I can see a scrying sensor.

04:29:41.770 --> 04:29:43.290
Seeker: Oh, I didn't know that that was a thing.

04:29:43.350 --> 04:29:45.650
Unknown: Yeah. It's just a, it's like a eye.

04:29:46.010 --> 04:29:46.270
Unknown: Right.

04:29:46.270 --> 04:29:49.290
Kenzo: It's just an invisible eye. If you can see invisible, you can see the scrying sensor.

04:29:49.330 --> 04:29:49.610
Unknown: Wait, does the top still spin?

04:29:49.610 --> 04:29:51.490
Unknown: Yeah, I'm gonna, I'm gonna see invisible.

04:29:52.810 --> 04:29:53.610
Kenzo: Is the top still spinning?

04:29:54.430 --> 04:29:55.730
DM: Dimitar's looking at it.

04:29:55.770 --> 04:29:56.090
Unknown: Is there a-

04:29:56.090 --> 04:29:57.050
DM: What's it supposed to do?

04:29:57.610 --> 04:29:58.350
Unknown: Is there an eye?

04:29:59.030 --> 04:29:59.930
DM: No, there's not an eye.

04:30:00.630 --> 04:30:01.430
Unknown: Wait, wait. It's supposed to

04:30:02.950 --> 04:30:04.410
Wellby: s- spin if we're being watched?

04:30:04.730 --> 04:30:05.310
Unknown: It spins if anybody's watching.

04:30:05.370 --> 04:30:10.210
DM: It spins if it's being watched, but everybody has to turn their back and wait for it to fall down.

04:30:10.430 --> 04:30:10.630
Unknown: Oh, yeah.

04:30:10.630 --> 04:30:12.090
DM: Dimitar doesn't quite get the picture.

04:30:12.310 --> 04:30:14.130
Wellby: Y- you gotta clo- close your eyes, Dimitar.

04:30:14.210 --> 04:30:15.870
Wellby: It, it detects if we're being scried.

04:30:16.370 --> 04:30:18.630
DM: Wait, why? It seems like it spins on its own.

04:30:18.630 --> 04:30:22.090
DM: I'd call it something like a always spinning top.

04:30:22.790 --> 04:30:23.030
Unknown: Yeah.

04:30:23.150 --> 04:30:24.730
Wellby: Yeah, but only if you look at it.

04:30:24.730 --> 04:30:27.810
Delwath: If you walk away, it'll fall over unless somebody else is looking.

04:30:28.750 --> 04:30:30.650
Seeker: If anybody's looking at it, it keeps spinning.

04:30:30.730 --> 04:30:32.050
DM: Okay, let's all do a test.

04:30:32.830 --> 04:30:33.490
Unknown: Mm-hmm.

04:30:33.490 --> 04:30:36.410
DM: Everybody turn their back. I'll close my eyes and we'll see what happens.

04:30:36.410 --> 04:30:37.150
DM: Listen for it.

04:30:38.050 --> 04:30:38.670
Unknown: Okay.

04:30:38.790 --> 04:30:39.150
Unknown: Yeah.

04:30:40.990 --> 04:30:41.850
DM: It keeps spinning.

04:30:42.450 --> 04:30:44.330
Wellby: Are your eyes really closed, Dimitar?

04:30:44.490 --> 04:30:46.490
DM: No. [laughs]

04:30:46.490 --> 04:30:46.770
Unknown: Yeah, they were.

04:30:46.770 --> 04:30:48.950
Wellby: Yeah, Dimitar, actually close your eyes this time.

04:30:50.510 --> 04:30:51.930
DM: He closes his eyes. It falls down.

04:30:51.950 --> 04:30:52.890
Unknown: No, all, all the way.

04:30:52.890 --> 04:30:53.670
DM: It falls down.

04:30:54.050 --> 04:30:55.570
Delwath: But I can see there's no scrying sensor.

04:30:55.810 --> 04:30:57.050
DM: Then he opens his eyes a peek.

04:30:57.150 --> 04:30:58.850
DM: Oh, wow. It stands up on its own.

04:31:00.490 --> 04:31:02.570
DM: Do, do, do you need this?

04:31:02.570 --> 04:31:03.150
Unknown: [laughs] Yeah.

04:31:06.430 --> 04:31:06.870
DM: Really?

04:31:07.510 --> 04:31:09.650
Kenzo: We'll give it to you later after we kill Apollyon.

04:31:09.650 --> 04:31:10.990
Kenzo: It's yours. Promise.

04:31:12.270 --> 04:31:12.630
DM: Okay.

04:31:13.530 --> 04:31:14.670
Seeker: We've, we've been spies for so long.

04:31:14.690 --> 04:31:16.370
Wellby: He's not in power to make this deal-

04:31:16.370 --> 04:31:16.970
Unknown: [laughs]

04:31:16.970 --> 04:31:18.190
Wellby: ... on behalf of all of us.

04:31:18.850 --> 04:31:19.350
Unknown: After we kill Apollyon.

04:31:19.390 --> 04:31:21.070
DM: Why not? He looks like the strong one.

04:31:22.150 --> 04:31:22.170
Unknown: Uh.

04:31:22.230 --> 04:31:23.150
DM: Or maybe him.

04:31:24.490 --> 04:31:24.630
Unknown: I mean

04:31:26.562 --> 04:31:26.722
Unknown: Oh.

04:31:28.042 --> 04:31:29.362
Unknown: Huh. Huh.

04:31:30.702 --> 04:31:33.722
Unknown: I think Kenzo deserves to make decisions about the top.

04:31:33.722 --> 04:31:42.822
Kenzo: Look, the point is, Dimitar, we were successful in bringing together the hand of your former friend and ally.

04:31:43.622 --> 04:31:47.442
Kenzo: Um, we completed a very, very complex quest to get this thing done.

04:31:48.302 --> 04:31:48.602
Unknown: Also-

04:31:48.682 --> 04:31:49.902
DM: That seems awesome for you.

04:31:50.182 --> 04:31:50.302
Unknown: Huh?

04:31:50.542 --> 04:31:52.002
DM: I said that seems awesome for you.

04:31:52.202 --> 04:31:58.322
Kenzo: For us. For us collectively, as you share in a similar goal and vision.

04:31:59.542 --> 04:32:01.062
Kenzo: Uh, also, um,

04:32:02.302 --> 04:32:07.382
Kenzo: we, uh, we, we freed, uh, or we, we have a, a giant crystal with a, uh

04:32:08.202 --> 04:32:10.242
Unknown: Cloudspinner person inside. Yeah, an ancient archfey.

04:32:10.282 --> 04:32:11.962
Wellby: Yeah. Who's been imprisoned for millennium.

04:32:12.002 --> 04:32:12.122
Unknown: Yeah.

04:32:12.242 --> 04:32:13.422
DM: Oh.

04:32:14.102 --> 04:32:14.442
Unknown: Yeah, yeah.

04:32:15.542 --> 04:32:15.622
Unknown: What?

04:32:15.682 --> 04:32:17.602
DM: That makes sense now.

04:32:17.842 --> 04:32:18.462
Unknown: Yeah, yeah, she's here.

04:32:19.462 --> 04:32:21.802
DM: Oh, she's gonna be so pissed.

04:32:21.842 --> 04:32:23.722
Unknown: Yeah, yeah. But she's here. Remember when we...

04:32:23.722 --> 04:32:25.282
Unknown: Weren't you listening earlier?

04:32:25.342 --> 04:32:27.022
Unknown: Yeah. [laughs]

04:32:27.082 --> 04:32:28.742
DM: You didn't know about the Cloudspinner earlier.

04:32:28.862 --> 04:32:33.222
Unknown: No, no, no, no. When we came here, starting by saying the dragon is really bad.

04:32:33.422 --> 04:32:35.802
DM: Oh, yeah. Ha ha, this guy gets it.

04:32:37.062 --> 04:32:38.902
Delwath: Um, here, uh,

04:32:40.342 --> 04:32:42.522
Delwath: I'm gonna scry Ragemptus.

04:32:46.162 --> 04:32:47.262
DM: Uh, it doesn't work.

04:32:48.942 --> 04:32:50.522
DM: She went into her lair.

04:32:50.522 --> 04:32:51.682
DM: Scrying across planes.

04:32:51.682 --> 04:32:53.322
Unknown: But how can she scry across planes?

04:32:54.642 --> 04:32:55.922
DM: Her lair is magic.

04:32:55.922 --> 04:33:06.442
Unknown: [snapping fingers] Anyways, uh, so there's probably

04:33:06.442 --> 04:33:10.362
Kenzo: like monsters, maybe hordes of monsters headed here.

04:33:11.862 --> 04:33:12.642
Unknown: Um...

04:33:12.642 --> 04:33:16.002
DM: I mean, it's not gonna be instantaneous.

04:33:16.322 --> 04:33:17.662
Kenzo: Yeah. We're, that's... We're gonna rest, right?

04:33:17.662 --> 04:33:19.142
DM: She's gotta scry the whole island.

04:33:19.142 --> 04:33:20.642
DM: She can't just see it all at once.

04:33:20.702 --> 04:33:22.242
Kenzo: Exactly. So we have time.

04:33:22.242 --> 04:33:27.322
Seeker: Should keep an eye out through the window just in case the chimeras do fly straight for us at some point.

04:33:27.482 --> 04:33:28.042
DM: Um...

04:33:29.282 --> 04:33:30.482
DM: What's like maybe highest?

04:33:30.662 --> 04:33:34.642
DM: I'm gonna suggest maybe sleeping in the tunnels.

04:33:35.242 --> 04:33:36.802
Unknown: I like this idea. That's a great idea.

04:33:37.682 --> 04:33:39.482
DM: I mean, I never sleep out in the open.

04:33:39.482 --> 04:33:40.622
DM: Only fools do that.

04:33:40.622 --> 04:33:43.302
Kenzo: [laughs] Yeah, we weren't thinking about doing that.

04:33:44.062 --> 04:33:46.002
Kenzo: Um, [clears throat] that's a great idea.

04:33:46.002 --> 04:33:46.702
Unknown: Why don't we go do that?

04:33:46.782 --> 04:33:48.822
DM: It's a little tight.

04:33:49.462 --> 04:33:51.042
DM: You'll, you two will be fine.

04:33:52.162 --> 04:33:53.722
DM: How do you feel about tight spaces?

04:33:53.722 --> 04:33:55.662
DM: Any claustrophobia?

04:33:55.722 --> 04:33:56.122
Unknown: It's fine.

04:33:57.622 --> 04:33:57.982
DM: Okay.

04:34:00.102 --> 04:34:00.382
DM: Um-

04:34:00.602 --> 04:34:02.362
Kenzo: As long as I don't have to cuddle with the elf, I'm fine.

04:34:03.042 --> 04:34:04.782
DM: Oh, no. You can all be in a row.

04:34:05.322 --> 04:34:05.602
Unknown: All right.

04:34:07.302 --> 04:34:07.702
DM: But, uh,

04:34:09.082 --> 04:34:09.422
DM: hmm.

04:34:12.062 --> 04:34:13.322
Unknown: Where's the entrance to these tunnels?

04:34:15.662 --> 04:34:18.142
DM: This is the trap door behind the statue.

04:34:18.202 --> 04:34:20.222
Unknown: Okay.

04:34:20.222 --> 04:34:22.182
Wellby: Should someone be keeping lookout?

04:34:22.182 --> 04:34:24.382
Delwath: I might wait out here.

04:34:27.602 --> 04:34:30.862
Delwath: A, I don't actually need a long rest.

04:34:34.142 --> 04:34:37.062
Delwath: And B, I only need four hours to get a long rest.

04:34:41.862 --> 04:34:42.962
Unknown: Awesome. Whatever you like.

04:34:42.982 --> 04:34:43.822
DM: It's up to you.

04:34:44.242 --> 04:34:45.762
Delwath: I mean, it's a little tight, right?

04:34:47.482 --> 04:34:48.322
DM: I mean,

04:34:49.422 --> 04:34:52.202
DM: yeah, but when she scrys you,

04:34:53.002 --> 04:34:54.282
DM: what do you think she's gonna do?

04:34:56.782 --> 04:34:59.022
Unknown: But can she not scry in the tunnels?

04:35:00.682 --> 04:35:02.502
Kenzo: But when she does, she just sees a bunch of tunnels.

04:35:04.422 --> 04:35:04.662
Unknown: Unless she-

04:35:04.722 --> 04:35:05.562
DM: I mean...

04:35:07.482 --> 04:35:12.062
Delwath: If she can scry us physically, specifically us, it's not gonna take her any time.

04:35:13.422 --> 04:35:15.382
DM: Uh, no, she can scry the island.

04:35:15.462 --> 04:35:15.982
Unknown: Yeah, yeah. That's what I said.

04:35:15.982 --> 04:35:17.302
DM: Any location on the island.

04:35:18.342 --> 04:35:18.742
Unknown: But can she scry-

04:35:18.742 --> 04:35:19.962
DM: That was what Dimitar was saying.

04:35:20.002 --> 04:35:23.342
Delwath: Yeah, no, I got that. But can she scry inside the temple?

04:35:23.422 --> 04:35:24.102
DM: I mean,

04:35:25.222 --> 04:35:27.162
Unknown: probably. She's aware of it.

04:35:27.162 --> 04:35:27.282
Unknown: So, so-

04:35:27.282 --> 04:35:30.602
DM: She might not be aware... Dimitar doesn't think she's aware of its tunnels.

04:35:31.362 --> 04:35:32.942
Delwath: So she probably can't scry inside the tunnel.

04:35:32.942 --> 04:35:33.802
Unknown: Let's all go in the tunnels.

04:35:33.842 --> 04:35:34.642
DM: Yeah, let's go in the tunnels.

04:35:34.702 --> 04:35:39.582
Kenzo: I like it. Yeah. [clears throat] That feels like a great thing to do.

04:35:39.582 --> 04:35:43.622
Kenzo: Hey, you seem to say, seem to know something about the person, uh, trapped inside the, uh-

04:35:43.662 --> 04:35:45.962
DM: No, I don't, but it all clicked into place.

04:35:47.162 --> 04:35:48.381
DM: I knew the story.

04:35:48.842 --> 04:35:49.402
Unknown: Which story?

04:35:50.062 --> 04:35:51.002
DM: That Shemut

04:35:52.242 --> 04:36:03.162
DM: captured some powerful archfey who refused to give him the secrets of divinity that he wanted to use to

04:36:03.162 --> 04:36:07.622
DM: kill the gods, and that Apollyon wanted to use to become a god.

04:36:08.402 --> 04:36:08.602
Unknown: Oh.

04:36:08.622 --> 04:36:11.122
DM: And they fought over what it, whoever this was,

04:36:12.542 --> 04:36:13.662
DM: and Shemut won,

04:36:15.282 --> 04:36:17.962
DM: but Apollyon got away with some magic item.

04:36:17.962 --> 04:36:19.022
DM: I don't know what it was.

04:36:20.942 --> 04:36:22.242
DM: That must have been what

04:36:23.482 --> 04:36:27.442
DM: Ragemptus has been guarding this whole time, the thing that

04:36:28.502 --> 04:36:32.442
DM: Shemut was trying to use to learn how to kill the gods.

04:36:33.422 --> 04:36:33.642
Unknown: Hmm.

04:36:35.362 --> 04:36:37.782
DM: What did you say? Who did you say it was?

04:36:37.782 --> 04:36:39.222
Unknown: Cloudspinner.

04:36:39.222 --> 04:36:40.202
DM: I don't know who that is.

04:36:41.702 --> 04:36:43.382
Delwath: Who it was. It's the person.

04:36:43.382 --> 04:36:43.942
Delwath: It's her name.

04:36:44.122 --> 04:36:46.302
DM: That's her name. Ah, okay.

04:36:46.302 --> 04:36:47.422
DM: That's a good fey name.

04:36:49.602 --> 04:36:52.202
Kenzo: So why did Ragemptus use Cloudspinner for herself?

04:36:52.202 --> 04:36:54.402
Kenzo: I mean, Shemut's been dead for hundreds of years.

04:36:56.402 --> 04:36:59.462
Kenzo: Like, why is she still, why is she still, why she been still guarding it this whole time?

04:37:00.642 --> 04:37:01.262
Kenzo: For what purpose?

04:37:01.702 --> 04:37:02.262
DM: I don't know.

04:37:03.922 --> 04:37:05.302
Seeker: Perhaps it's a curse upon her.

04:37:06.442 --> 04:37:06.642
DM: I mean-

04:37:06.722 --> 04:37:07.942
Kenzo: I can ask her when she, she shows up.

04:37:08.962 --> 04:37:12.182
DM: Maybe she is unable to disobey Shemut's command.

04:37:13.082 --> 04:37:17.062
Delwath: Oh, that's interesting. What's the theory of why we would be here when she shows up exactly?

04:37:19.182 --> 04:37:19.642
Unknown: What do you mean?

04:37:20.562 --> 04:37:23.742
Delwath: Like, why wouldn't we just teleport away?

04:37:24.222 --> 04:37:25.182
DM: After you long rest?

04:37:25.482 --> 04:37:26.082
Unknown: Yeah. Yeah.

04:37:26.502 --> 04:37:29.322
DM: Wait, you're gonna leave me to be slaughtered by a dragon?

04:37:29.382 --> 04:37:30.862
Kenzo: You're coming with us. You're coming with us.

04:37:30.862 --> 04:37:33.682
DM: You're gonna leave the dragonets to be slaughtered by a dragon?

04:37:34.042 --> 04:37:34.922
Unknown: Why would she kill them?

04:37:35.394 --> 04:37:39.554
Wellby: 'Cause they brought us to her and like vouched for us and-

04:37:39.554 --> 04:37:41.634
DM: Have you never fought like a dragon before?

04:37:42.574 --> 04:37:46.074
DM: She's gonna kill everybody on this island if she doesn't get the Cloudspinner back.

04:37:47.254 --> 04:37:47.994
Unknown: Uh.

04:37:48.154 --> 04:37:53.774
Delwath: Uh. [sighs] I guess we have to be heroes.

04:37:56.714 --> 04:37:59.154
DM: I mean, how many people can you teleport?

04:38:00.574 --> 04:38:00.814
Unknown: Eight.

04:38:01.774 --> 04:38:02.894
DM: Oh, well, that's useless.

04:38:03.634 --> 04:38:04.054
Unknown: Why is that?

04:38:05.134 --> 04:38:05.914
DM: I mean, there's at least

04:38:08.174 --> 04:38:09.454
DM: 50 I'd wanna rescue.

04:38:09.454 --> 04:38:14.774
Kenzo: [clears throat] This is gonna make the airship really fun later.

04:38:14.774 --> 04:38:15.074
DM: There's a, there's a-

04:38:15.114 --> 04:38:16.094
Unknown: Well, not if we kill the dragon today

04:38:16.094 --> 04:38:18.214
DM: ... there's like 100 we could just let die.

04:38:18.214 --> 04:38:18.994
DM: That'd be fine.

04:38:19.954 --> 04:38:21.534
Kenzo: Wait, but what about the ones that are loyal to her?

04:38:21.554 --> 04:38:22.494
Unknown: She's gonna kill them too?

04:38:23.894 --> 04:38:27.794
DM: She might. Have you ever seen a really, truly pissed dragon?

04:38:27.894 --> 04:38:27.994
Wellby: Yeah.

04:38:28.014 --> 04:38:28.574
Kenzo: I mean, yeah.

04:38:30.054 --> 04:38:30.754
Unknown: We've killed a couple.

04:38:31.614 --> 04:38:33.894
DM: Oh, that's great, actually. Then you're definitely staying.

04:38:33.894 --> 04:38:38.334
Seeker: [sighs] [clears throat] Smaller ones.

04:38:38.334 --> 04:38:40.254
Seeker: We've killed mostly slightly smaller ones.

04:38:41.094 --> 04:38:42.574
Kenzo: Where do you think we should fight her?

04:38:42.574 --> 04:38:42.874
DM: Well,

04:38:43.734 --> 04:38:46.034
DM: it's always time to step up in the world, right?

04:38:46.054 --> 04:38:47.714
Kenzo: So Dimitar, where do you think we should fight her?

04:38:47.714 --> 04:38:49.514
Kenzo: We meaning the four, the five of us together.

04:38:49.574 --> 04:38:50.434
DM: Wait, can you fly?

04:38:50.814 --> 04:38:51.594
Kenzo: Yeah.

04:38:51.594 --> 04:38:52.214
DM: All of you?

04:38:52.294 --> 04:38:52.834
Wellby: Yep.

04:38:52.934 --> 04:38:54.154
Unknown: Ish. Sort of.

04:38:54.534 --> 04:38:54.734
Unknown: Yeah.

04:38:55.034 --> 04:38:55.994
DM: Close enough.

04:38:56.054 --> 04:38:57.074
Unknown: Yeah.

04:38:57.194 --> 04:38:59.434
DM: Um, 'cause, you know,

04:39:00.634 --> 04:39:01.934
DM: she's probably not gonna land.

04:39:03.674 --> 04:39:03.954
Unknown: Yeah.

04:39:09.234 --> 04:39:10.234
Seeker: Air combat, huh?

04:39:10.274 --> 04:39:10.574
Wellby: Yeah.

04:39:11.134 --> 04:39:12.974
Seeker: Oh, I have a rules question, Tim.

04:39:13.594 --> 04:39:15.054
Seeker: I thought I saw something about

04:39:16.074 --> 04:39:20.594
Seeker: long rest while waking, while being able to do things that require being awake,

04:39:21.754 --> 04:39:22.554
Seeker: like a special ability.

04:39:22.934 --> 04:39:23.454
DM: Like what?

04:39:24.634 --> 04:39:26.314
Seeker: That I could have a long rest while being awake.

04:39:26.654 --> 04:39:27.974
Unknown: Oh, simulacrum.

04:39:28.094 --> 04:39:32.094
DM: Oh. Um, no, you can't have a long rest unless...

04:39:32.654 --> 04:39:33.854
DM: What special ability is this?

04:39:35.214 --> 04:39:40.534
Seeker: Something that I was reading a lot of stuff on my character sheet, and I remember seeing that, but maybe that was a spell.

04:39:42.554 --> 04:39:42.774
DM: I don't know.

04:39:42.774 --> 04:39:44.854
Delwath: You might have a potion or something that lets you do that.

04:39:45.093 --> 04:39:46.394
Delwath: Oh, you... I think you might have.

04:39:46.394 --> 04:39:47.934
Unknown: Go check your, check your character sheet.

04:39:48.574 --> 04:39:49.674
Delwath: Tim might have something there as a-

04:39:49.714 --> 04:39:51.594
DM: You have a potion of watchful rest.

04:39:52.254 --> 04:39:52.874
Unknown: That's what it is.

04:39:53.074 --> 04:39:53.674
Unknown: Yeah.

04:39:53.674 --> 04:39:56.514
DM: Yeah. But simulacrum takes 12 hours.

04:39:56.514 --> 04:39:57.294
DM: [chuckles]

04:39:57.294 --> 04:39:58.214
Unknown: How long is a long rest?

04:39:58.714 --> 04:40:01.794
