05:04:00.558 --> 05:04:01.198
Unknown: Anti-magic

05:04:01.198 --> 05:04:01.318
Unknown: ... anti-magic?

05:04:01.378 --> 05:04:02.617
DM: Anti-magic.

05:04:02.638 --> 05:04:03.538
Kenzo: We have to get back to the ship.

05:04:04.078 --> 05:04:04.638
Unknown: Yeah.

05:04:04.638 --> 05:04:05.678
Kenzo: I guess we fly there anyways.

05:04:06.558 --> 05:04:07.338
Unknown: We'll have the ship with us.

05:04:08.058 --> 05:04:09.578
Seeker: We don't, we don't have time, probably.

05:04:10.158 --> 05:04:11.598
Wellby: How far is it from here to there?

05:04:11.618 --> 05:04:13.138
Unknown: We're, we're close to Dranikor right now, right?

05:04:13.478 --> 05:04:13.838
Unknown: Maybe two hours.

05:04:13.898 --> 05:04:14.858
Unknown: It'd be a couple hundred miles.

05:04:16.298 --> 05:04:17.738
DM: Yeah, you're pretty close to Dranikor.

05:04:18.038 --> 05:04:18.778
DM: I mean, this was a-

05:04:19.958 --> 05:04:20.818
Seeker: We do want the ship with us.

05:04:20.878 --> 05:04:25.338
DM: You're like, um, you're probably no mo- You're definitely no more than 200 miles.

05:04:25.338 --> 05:04:26.638
DM: That's 20 hours.

05:04:26.638 --> 05:04:27.458
DM: That's less than a day.

05:04:27.518 --> 05:04:30.198
Seeker: Also, like, Vindristjarna versus

05:04:32.378 --> 05:04:34.778
Seeker: vast domed structure, we could probably take it.

05:04:36.798 --> 05:04:37.038
DM: Yeah.

05:04:37.378 --> 05:04:38.738
Seeker: Puncture the dome and shit.

05:04:39.058 --> 05:04:41.578
Delwath: I mean, the first thing we're gonna have to do is defeat our own doppelgangers.

05:04:42.238 --> 05:04:43.418
Delwath: But wait, they can't level up.

05:04:44.238 --> 05:04:44.638
DM: Right.

05:04:44.638 --> 05:04:45.578
Unknown: [laughs]

05:04:45.598 --> 05:04:47.778
DM: It's true. They don't have eighth level slots.

05:04:47.818 --> 05:04:48.218
Unknown: Nice.

05:04:50.218 --> 05:04:52.198
Seeker: Are there a lot more of those, we think?

05:04:52.998 --> 05:04:53.778
Delwath: There's one of each of us.

05:04:53.818 --> 05:04:54.658
DM: There's one of each of you.

05:04:55.058 --> 05:04:55.518
Unknown: Remember, they all have eighth level-

05:04:55.578 --> 05:04:58.438
DM: Oh, but Seeker's the only one who has eighth level slots, so...

05:04:58.438 --> 05:05:00.698
Unknown: But none of them have eighth level slots.

05:05:00.718 --> 05:05:03.138
Seeker: And, uh, they haven't been destroyed.

05:05:03.758 --> 05:05:06.358
Delwath: No, they all died once, and then we start this again.

05:05:06.398 --> 05:05:14.498
DM: They all wear some amulet, so when you fight them, you have to take the amulet off them before you kill them, otherwise they just reform again.

05:05:14.738 --> 05:05:15.058
Unknown: Right.

05:05:15.978 --> 05:05:17.858
Unknown: Oh, man.

05:05:17.858 --> 05:05:19.018
DM: Well, that's for another time.

05:05:19.378 --> 05:05:19.558
Unknown: Yep.

05:05:21.218 --> 05:05:21.458
DM: So,

05:05:22.878 --> 05:05:23.058
DM: uh,

05:05:23.898 --> 05:05:25.498
DM: okay, let's see what happens.

05:05:25.498 --> 05:05:25.818
DM: Um,

05:05:27.478 --> 05:05:28.778
DM: at about...

05:05:28.778 --> 05:05:30.498
DM: So what happens if the lynx is triggered?

05:05:31.298 --> 05:05:32.038
Unknown: It's alarm spell.

05:05:32.338 --> 05:05:33.538
DM: Okay.

05:05:33.538 --> 05:05:36.058
Delwath: So it's, it's mental currently.

05:05:36.158 --> 05:05:36.338
DM: Okay.

05:05:36.338 --> 05:05:38.298
Unknown: I can choose whether it's noise or mental, but it's mental.

05:05:38.498 --> 05:05:39.758
DM: So at about,

05:05:40.938 --> 05:05:41.178
DM: um,

05:05:42.678 --> 05:05:43.478
DM: maybe

05:05:44.978 --> 05:05:45.738
DM: 1:00 in the morning,

05:05:48.138 --> 05:05:51.478
DM: um, the alarm spell is trig- You don't, do you know what triggers it?

05:05:52.318 --> 05:05:54.998
Unknown: I think so, but I'm not sure.

05:05:55.058 --> 05:05:56.658
Unknown: I may, probab- I don't know, maybe not.

05:05:57.038 --> 05:05:59.178
Wellby: 1:00 in the morning is a full long rest, right?

05:06:00.818 --> 05:06:00.998
DM: Uh-

05:06:01.038 --> 05:06:01.718
Unknown: Starting at what?

05:06:04.818 --> 05:06:05.298
DM: 5:00 to-

05:06:06.258 --> 05:06:07.078
Unknown: Only four hours.

05:06:08.918 --> 05:06:10.498
Unknown: 5:00 to 1:00? Yeah, that's...

05:06:12.198 --> 05:06:13.597
DM: No, that's not eight hours, is it?

05:06:15.477 --> 05:06:15.958
Unknown: Yeah, it is.

05:06:15.958 --> 05:06:16.458
Unknown: I don't know.

05:06:17.038 --> 05:06:19.418
DM: Oh yeah, it is eight hours. Yeah, that's a full long rest.

05:06:20.998 --> 05:06:21.318
DM: Um...

05:06:23.338 --> 05:06:24.078
Delwath: It doesn't tell me who's-

05:06:24.158 --> 05:06:29.838
DM: It doesn't... So, okay, at about 1:00, you've all completed a long rest, but the spell is not finished,

05:06:30.858 --> 05:06:31.118
DM: and

05:06:32.898 --> 05:06:34.718
DM: the spell still needs another four hours.

05:06:34.718 --> 05:06:35.678
DM: The alarm is triggered.

05:06:35.938 --> 05:06:36.458
Unknown: What spell?

05:06:37.178 --> 05:06:39.298
DM: Some arc- Oh no, you're not doing some arcane cantrip.

05:06:39.298 --> 05:06:39.378
Unknown: We can't do it.

05:06:39.378 --> 05:06:40.058
DM: Okay, 1:00 AM.

05:06:40.078 --> 05:06:40.618
Unknown: What spell is it?

05:06:40.618 --> 05:06:43.718
DM: I forgot. 1:00 AM, the spell, the alarm is triggered.

05:06:46.398 --> 05:06:48.338
Seeker: Just at the moment we could have started doing something.

05:06:49.838 --> 05:06:51.438
Unknown: Like, we got like eight hours of sleep, right?

05:06:51.438 --> 05:06:52.518
DM: Yeah.

05:06:52.558 --> 05:06:53.298
Unknown: We long rested.

05:06:54.378 --> 05:06:58.638
Delwath: But it's probably Tilly and Milo, not, uh, Frank, we hope.

05:06:59.338 --> 05:07:01.178
Wellby: Can we see what triggered it?

05:07:02.018 --> 05:07:03.278
DM: You can climb out of the tunnel.

05:07:05.258 --> 05:07:06.818
Wellby: I climb out of the tunnel very carefully.

05:07:06.818 --> 05:07:08.278
Kenzo: Is Dimitar in the tunnel with us this whole time?

05:07:08.338 --> 05:07:08.938
DM: Oh, yeah.

05:07:08.958 --> 05:07:09.558
Unknown: Huh?

05:07:09.558 --> 05:07:11.198
DM: No, he sleeps curled up in the statue.

05:07:11.378 --> 05:07:12.958
Wellby: There's a, there's a people out of the tunnel.

05:07:13.358 --> 05:07:15.698
DM: Out of the statue, that's right. You can go out into the, um-

05:07:15.718 --> 05:07:16.938
Seeker: You can see into the temple at least

05:07:16.938 --> 05:07:22.558
DM: ... um, there is a pair of dragonets

05:07:24.498 --> 05:07:26.518
DM: that are just kind of sitting in the temple,

05:07:28.318 --> 05:07:31.438
DM: kind of curious about just keeping an eye.

05:07:34.178 --> 05:07:34.578
Unknown: Wait, Dimitar-

05:07:34.718 --> 05:07:35.918
Unknown: It'd be really funny to use the god's voice.

05:07:35.918 --> 05:07:38.438
Unknown: Do you know them?

05:07:38.438 --> 05:07:39.838
Delwath: I... Does Dimitar know these dragonets?

05:07:40.278 --> 05:07:40.398
DM: Nope.

05:07:43.578 --> 05:07:45.378
Seeker: Can we hear them if they talk?

05:07:45.438 --> 05:07:45.678
DM: Yeah.

05:07:46.778 --> 05:07:47.598
Unknown: Can you Soul Sight them?

05:07:48.338 --> 05:07:48.618
Unknown: Sure.

05:07:49.158 --> 05:07:50.038
Unknown: That's free, right?

05:07:50.078 --> 05:07:50.238
DM: Yeah.

05:07:51.678 --> 05:07:52.118
DM: Um-

05:07:52.698 --> 05:07:53.898
Seeker: We're keeping very quiet

05:07:53.898 --> 05:07:57.698
DM: ... they're, I mean, they're just, they're watchful.

05:07:58.958 --> 05:08:00.258
DM: They're sort of bored.

05:08:00.258 --> 05:08:00.838
Unknown: What's CR?

05:08:01.838 --> 05:08:02.098
DM: Two.

05:08:07.248 --> 05:08:08.348
Wellby: Do we just sleep?

05:08:09.108 --> 05:08:10.168
Seeker: That's what I'd like to suggest.

05:08:10.448 --> 05:08:10.628
Wellby: Yeah.

05:08:11.708 --> 05:08:12.268
Unknown: Going to sleep.

05:08:20.728 --> 05:08:22.148
DM: I think that's like a wisdom save.

05:08:22.728 --> 05:08:23.168
Unknown: No save.

05:08:24.068 --> 05:08:25.208
DM: No, the spell changed.

05:08:25.248 --> 05:08:28.208
Delwath: Oh, come on. The new s- the new sleep spell is the dumbest...

05:08:28.928 --> 05:08:29.208
Wellby: What is it?

05:08:29.228 --> 05:08:30.848
Delwath: It's literally the worst spell in the world.

05:08:30.908 --> 05:08:30.968
DM: Oh, well.

05:08:30.968 --> 05:08:33.328
DM: I would assume you'd use the existing sleep or whatever.

05:08:33.348 --> 05:08:34.948
DM: I didn't read the new sleep spell.

05:08:34.948 --> 05:08:36.848
Unknown: The new sleep spell's stupid.

05:08:38.068 --> 05:08:41.088
Delwath: It's like literally an idiotic spell that you would never take.

05:08:42.528 --> 05:08:43.528
Seeker: Why does it work?

05:08:43.528 --> 05:08:46.048
Delwath: Well, the old sleep spell is super fun because it's all about hit points.

05:08:46.048 --> 05:08:46.048
Wellby: Right.

05:08:46.068 --> 05:08:48.228
Unknown: It's like designed to knock down.

05:08:48.688 --> 05:08:51.308
Delwath: The new sleep spell is just a wisdom save or nothing happens to you.

05:08:51.308 --> 05:08:54.008
Unknown: It's-- And even if you make your wisdom save, you don't even fall asleep.

05:08:57.928 --> 05:08:58.048
Wellby: Hmm.

05:09:00.068 --> 05:09:00.128
Unknown: It-

05:09:00.148 --> 05:09:01.868
DM: Well, I mean, it's the same.

05:09:01.868 --> 05:09:09.008
DM: I mean, sleep, the sleep spell doesn't last, it doesn't make you fall asleep, but it still only lasts for a minute, the old sleep.

05:09:09.447 --> 05:09:10.528
Unknown: It does make you fall asleep.

05:09:11.048 --> 05:09:12.528
DM: But you wake up when the spell ends.

05:09:12.548 --> 05:09:13.848
Delwath: You wake up when the spell ends, yes.

05:09:14.408 --> 05:09:15.828
DM: So it's the sa- it's the same thing.

05:09:15.828 --> 05:09:18.828
DM: It's just too safe. It's useful in different contexts.

05:09:19.008 --> 05:09:20.228
Delwath: It's a double save.

05:09:21.548 --> 05:09:27.148
Delwath: But so what I always liked about the sleep spell is that it, the whole point of the sleep spell is it doesn't require a save.

05:09:30.288 --> 05:09:32.228
DM: I, I don't really care which way or the other.

05:09:32.228 --> 05:09:33.268
DM: No, I much rather keep the old sleep spell.

05:09:33.268 --> 05:09:38.408
DM: I mean, there's no way that a CR two creature is making two wisdom saves against a...

05:09:39.968 --> 05:09:40.028
Unknown: Yeah.

05:09:40.028 --> 05:09:42.168
DM: It has the roughly the same effect.

05:09:42.568 --> 05:09:43.928
Delwath: No, but it's much more useful.

05:09:43.928 --> 05:09:46.088
Delwath: Like the situation I actually used sleep was to-

05:09:46.168 --> 05:09:48.968
DM: Is when you take down enemies right at the very end.

05:09:49.388 --> 05:09:49.608
DM: Yeah, yeah.

05:09:49.608 --> 05:09:50.928
Unknown: It was taking on Kagdurs. It was taking on Kagdurs that-

05:09:50.928 --> 05:09:52.148
DM: That would be harder to do.

05:09:52.188 --> 05:09:53.728
Delwath: That's much harder to deal with.

05:09:56.468 --> 05:09:58.048
Unknown: I, I do not like the new sleep spell.

05:09:58.048 --> 05:09:58.288
Unknown: I forgot about it.

05:09:58.328 --> 05:10:00.408
DM: Yeah, it's not even a... Oh, it's a sorcerer spell.

05:10:01.348 --> 05:10:01.668
DM: Right.

05:10:02.588 --> 05:10:05.088
Unknown: Well, I have it for free from the Neswat, from the Neswat.

05:10:05.088 --> 05:10:05.228
DM: Yeah,

05:10:07.228 --> 05:10:08.988
DM: yeah. Uh, they fall asleep for a minute.

05:10:08.988 --> 05:10:09.628
DM: [thudding]

05:10:09.628 --> 05:10:11.068
Delwath: Well, I... Hold on.

05:10:11.068 --> 05:10:12.467
Delwath: We need a plan before we cast sleep.

05:10:13.828 --> 05:10:14.148
Wellby: Um,

05:10:20.888 --> 05:10:25.548
Wellby: tie them up and release them at dawn to go report back.

05:10:25.548 --> 05:10:26.808
Wellby: I think so. Right.

05:10:26.808 --> 05:10:27.788
Wellby: So we can fight in the dark.

05:10:27.808 --> 05:10:29.888
Delwath: I think we drag them into the tunnels and tie them, yeah.

05:10:33.328 --> 05:10:33.628
DM: Okay.

05:10:34.708 --> 05:10:36.948
DM: You drag them in, you tie them up and drag them into the tunnels.

05:10:37.268 --> 05:10:39.768
Delwath: Ask them and interrogate them a little bit.

05:10:40.888 --> 05:10:41.888
Delwath: I'll try and scare them.

05:10:44.548 --> 05:10:45.968
DM: Okay. Let's... Hold on one sec.

05:10:45.968 --> 05:10:50.288
DM: [paper rustling] I mean,

05:10:53.268 --> 05:10:56.328
DM: they're, you know, they're kind of...

05:10:57.028 --> 05:10:58.388
Delwath: I just want them to tell me what their orders were.

05:10:58.388 --> 05:11:00.028
Delwath: I don't, they don't need to betray the dragon.

05:11:00.028 --> 05:11:01.708
Delwath: They don't need to do anything. Just what do you do?

05:11:01.708 --> 05:11:03.468
Delwath: Why'd you come here? What are you doing here?

05:11:03.468 --> 05:11:09.548
Delwath: We won't kill you. [paper rustling]

05:11:09.568 --> 05:11:09.608
DM: Um.

05:11:09.628 --> 05:11:13.728
Delwath: But you're not going anyf- anywhere for a while, and you got to spell why you came here.

05:11:13.728 --> 05:11:14.208
Unknown: That's it.

05:11:16.928 --> 05:11:18.388
DM: Uh, what language are they asking then?

05:11:20.408 --> 05:11:23.768
Delwath: They only speak, uh... Oh, I'd probably have to have to cast tongues.

05:11:23.768 --> 05:11:25.348
Delwath: Um, they don't speak Common, do they?

05:11:25.348 --> 05:11:26.368
DM: They don't speak Common.

05:11:31.068 --> 05:11:32.488
Delwath: I can, I, I'll just cast tongues.

05:11:32.488 --> 05:11:32.748
Unknown: It's fine.

05:11:32.848 --> 05:11:33.148
DM: Okay.

05:11:34.248 --> 05:11:35.308
DM: One sec. I'll be right back.

05:12:25.808 --> 05:12:27.768
DM: [sighs] [coughs] I mean, they're, they're like a bit freaked.

05:12:28.708 --> 05:12:30.788
DM: It's like everybody's up in arms.

05:12:33.168 --> 05:12:34.548
DM: All the dragonets have been sent

05:12:35.688 --> 05:12:37.008
DM: everywhere across the island.

05:12:38.168 --> 05:12:39.088
DM: We're to keep watch

05:12:41.548 --> 05:12:45.668
DM: and report back ev- in two hours if anything shows up.

05:12:50.008 --> 05:12:51.408
Delwath: And they don't report back.

05:12:56.748 --> 05:12:58.748
Delwath: So it's okay. Maybe it's okay if she just comes here in two hours.

05:12:58.748 --> 05:12:59.348
Delwath: What are we waiting for?

05:13:03.968 --> 05:13:08.308
Wellby: Are there any others posted to this area of the island, like this sector?

05:13:08.308 --> 05:13:09.628
Wellby: Where, where are the nearest ones?

05:13:10.328 --> 05:13:12.528
Wellby: Can we move to other buildings in this complex?

05:13:15.288 --> 05:13:16.588
DM: She was very mad. I don't know.

05:13:16.588 --> 05:13:17.348
DM: They're everywhere.

05:13:19.168 --> 05:13:21.028
Delwath: Did you fly over here with any, anybody else?

05:13:21.028 --> 05:13:23.248
Delwath: You guys come here and split up or just the two of you?

05:13:23.688 --> 05:13:24.368
DM: Ten of us.

05:13:29.208 --> 05:13:31.348
Delwath: There's probably ten covering the top of the monastery.

05:13:32.428 --> 05:13:34.088
Unknown: There's eight temples. Well, great.

05:13:34.088 --> 05:13:36.588
Wellby: In two hours, everybody else flies back.

05:13:36.588 --> 05:13:38.268
Wellby: We can move to one of the other buildings.

05:13:40.868 --> 05:13:42.028
Unknown: Why do we want to move to another building?

05:13:44.188 --> 05:13:47.868
Wellby: So she doesn't just come and breathe acid through the roof

05:13:49.308 --> 05:13:50.788
Wellby: and kill us while we're all waiting inside.

05:13:53.188 --> 05:13:53.728
Unknown: I mean, like

05:13:55.088 --> 05:13:55.708
Unknown: these people

05:13:57.228 --> 05:13:58.808
Delwath: think we're... We...

05:13:58.808 --> 05:13:59.788
Unknown: Yeah, sure.

05:14:02.568 --> 05:14:02.808
Unknown: Um,

05:14:04.408 --> 05:14:08.248
Delwath: I, I will, I will, uh, thank them for their honesty and tell them, um-

05:14:12.184 --> 05:14:12.984
Delwath: So are you, uh...

05:14:16.083 --> 05:14:16.284
Unknown: Um,

05:14:19.744 --> 05:14:23.064
Delwath: I'll ask them if they know either of our two f- Gresh- Gresher.

05:14:23.064 --> 05:14:23.564
Delwath: What's her name? M-

05:14:24.684 --> 05:14:25.084
DM: Megren?

05:14:25.164 --> 05:14:26.284
DM: Yeah.

05:14:26.284 --> 05:14:26.464
DM: No.

05:14:30.524 --> 05:14:31.144
Delwath: Are you, um,

05:14:32.024 --> 05:14:33.344
Delwath: are you one of the true believers?

05:14:34.184 --> 05:14:35.084
Delwath: Are you just scared of her?

05:14:36.024 --> 05:14:36.204
DM: Who?

05:14:40.404 --> 05:14:42.244
DM: Looks kind of confused by the question.

05:14:42.964 --> 05:14:43.204
Unknown: True believer.

05:14:43.204 --> 05:14:46.264
DM: We all believe she's the queen of the island.

05:14:48.244 --> 05:14:50.084
Delwath: When she's dead, are you gonna be happy or sad?

05:14:51.904 --> 05:14:52.784
DM: Surprised.

05:14:52.784 --> 05:15:02.944
Unknown: [laughs] I mean, as an aside, why don't we just tell these people to tell her we're waiting

05:15:02.944 --> 05:15:03.364
Unknown: for her here?

05:15:03.424 --> 05:15:03.604
DM: Sure.

05:15:03.904 --> 05:15:04.704
Unknown: And then not be here.

05:15:05.204 --> 05:15:05.444
Unknown: Wait. Uh,

05:15:06.424 --> 05:15:07.304
Kenzo: would we want to fight her, though?

05:15:07.924 --> 05:15:09.864
Delwath: Well, somewhere around here, but, but...

05:15:10.464 --> 05:15:10.964
Kenzo: What's our plan?

05:15:11.584 --> 05:15:13.524
Delwath: Well, we have two hours. We'll make it in a minute.

05:15:14.264 --> 05:15:15.284
Delwath: Okay. Um-

05:15:15.844 --> 05:15:16.464
Kenzo: And put some music.

05:15:16.983 --> 05:15:17.784
DM: Oh, yeah, yeah.

05:15:19.204 --> 05:15:23.944
Delwath: So I'm gonna, um, I'm gonna tell them we might have more to say in a bit.

05:15:25.744 --> 05:15:27.484
Delwath: You know, we'll go away from them.

05:15:29.264 --> 05:15:31.404
Unknown: Siri here. Let me know if I can help.

05:15:31.884 --> 05:15:33.204
Delwath: Um, I'm gonna

05:15:34.344 --> 05:15:35.724
Delwath: reset... I mean, I'll reset the links.

05:15:36.044 --> 05:15:37.744
DM: Uh, I don't think your...

05:15:37.744 --> 05:15:38.444
DM: Is your thing on?

05:15:38.964 --> 05:15:40.824
Kenzo: Uh, Schwartz, want me to pass away? Should be.

05:15:40.824 --> 05:15:49.684
Unknown: [gentle music]

05:15:49.724 --> 05:15:49.984
DM: There we

05:15:56.044 --> 05:15:56.904
DM: go. Reset the links?

05:15:57.244 --> 05:15:57.784
Unknown: Yeah.

